new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2d965d9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# smallpt — The browser edition
+
+Kevin Beason's smallpt C++ path tracer compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten.
+Open the site's index.html through any static hosting. Rendering runs on your
+device in a dedicated module Web Worker. No backend or special isolation headers
+are needed.
+
+The page renders automatically. Randomize & render changes wall and sphere
+colors and starts a fresh render. Palette, resolution, and quality changes also
+rerender. Save image downloads the current image as a PNG.
+
+## Build
+
+Requires Emscripten (em++) on PATH and Node.js.
+
+    npm run build
+
+The complete static site is emitted to dist/. Compiled artifacts are also kept
+in public/ so the root checkout can be statically hosted directly.
+
+## Checks
+
+    node --check app.js
+    node --check worker.js
+    node scripts/check-wasm.mjs
+
+The last command executes the actual compiled Wasm under Node with local asset
+loading, and checks rendering, color changes, opaque output, and heap growth.
+No server or browser is started.
+
+## Initial preview
+
+The initial image is generated by the same C++ renderer with a deterministic
+seed at 800 × 600 and 64 samples per pixel. To regenerate it:
+
+    g++ src/renderer.cpp -O3 -DSMALLPT_PREVIEW -o /tmp/smallpt-preview
+    /tmp/smallpt-preview
+    python3 scripts/encode-preview.py
+    npm run build
+
+## Source and attribution
+
+Original: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/
+The unmodified source is src/smallpt-original.cpp; the adapted renderer is
+src/renderer.cpp. The original MIT license is retained in src/LICENSE.txt.
+
+The adaptation replaces OpenMP and PPM output with progressive batches and an
+RGBA buffer, adds adjustable material colors, accumulates linear radiance across
+passes, and bounds recursive depth at 128 for stack safety. Mirror, glass,
+diffuse scattering, scene geometry, and the camera remain from smallpt.
